---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Privacy policy" description="What information Freedom On Own Terms collects, how it is used, and your choices.">
  <section class="container page-head">
    <h1>Privacy <span class="gradient-text">policy</span></h1>
    <p class="muted">Last updated: 3 November 2026</p>
  </section>

  <section class="container prose">
    <p>
      This policy explains how Freedom On Own Terms ("we", "us") handles information when you visit
      freedomonownterms.com (the "site"). We are based in India and welcome visitors from around the world. We aim to
      follow India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023, the EU and UK General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR),
      the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA), and other laws that apply to you.
    </p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Information you send us:</strong> if you email us, we receive your email address and whatever you choose to
        write. We use it only to reply to you.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Newsletter:</strong> if you subscribe, your email address is stored by our newsletter provider so we can
        send you the newsletter. You can unsubscribe at any time using the link in every email.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Technical data:</strong> like most websites, our hosting provider (GitHub Pages) and the font service we use
        (Google Fonts) may automatically log technical details such as your IP address, browser type, and the pages you
        request, to deliver and secure the site.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Visitor statistics:</strong> we use Cloudflare Web Analytics to count visits and see which pages are
        popular. It does not use cookies, does not track you across websites, and does not identify individual visitors.
        See <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Weather Planner:</strong> when you use the <a href="/weather/">AI Weather Planner</a>, the city you search
        for, or your approximate location if you choose to share it, is sent directly from your browser to
        <a href="https://open-meteo.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open-Meteo</a> to get the forecast. We
        don't receive or store it. Your last city and preferred units are saved only in your own browser.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not sell your personal information.</p>

    <h2>Cookies and advertising</h2>
    <p>
      The site does not currently set any cookies. If we add advertising in the future (for example Google AdSense), those third parties may use cookies to measure visits and show ads, including personalised ads. We
      will update this policy and, where required, ask for your consent first. You can learn how Google uses data at
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Affiliate links</h2>
    <p>
      Some links to tools are affiliate links. When you click one, the destination company may record that you came from
      our site so we can earn a commission. That company's own privacy policy applies on its website. See our
      <a href="/disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Links to other websites</h2>
    <p>
      News headlines and tool listings link to other websites. We are not responsible for their content or privacy
      practices.
    </p>

    <h2>Why we use your information</h2>
    <p>
      We reply to your emails and send the newsletter because you asked us to (your consent, which you can withdraw at
      any time). Hosting logs and cookie-free visitor statistics are used because we have a legitimate interest in
      running, securing and improving the site.
    </p>

    <h2>International transfers</h2>
    <p>
      Our service providers, including GitHub, Cloudflare and Google, may process data in the United States and other
      countries. They use safeguards such as standard contractual clauses to protect it.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Wherever you live, you can ask us to access, correct, delete, or receive a copy of personal information we hold
      about you, object to how we use it, or withdraw consent you have given, by emailing us. We will respond within 30
      days. If you are in the EU or UK, you can also complain to your local data protection authority. If you are in
      California, note that we do not sell or share your personal information.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      The site is intended for a general audience and is not directed at children under 13 (or the minimum age in your
      country). If you are under 18, please ask a parent or guardian before subscribing to the newsletter or sending us
      personal information. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children without that consent.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>We may update this policy. The "last updated" date at the top shows when it last changed.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Email <a href="mailto:hello@freedomonownterms.com">hello@freedomonownterms.com</a>.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
